From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] developertools: use QUnifiedTimer::setSpeedModifier for Qt
 6.12

  unifiedtimerwrapper.cpp:33:32: error: 'class QUnifiedTimer' has no member
  named 'setSlowModeEnabled'

QUnifiedTimer is Qt private API. Qt 6.12 dropped the slow-mode pair
(setSlowModeEnabled / setSlowdownFactor) in favour of one speed multiplier,
described in qabstractanimation_p.h as facilitating "both fine-tuning of
complex animations by slowing them down, and reducing execution time of auto
tests by speeding them up".

Qt's old default slowdown factor was 5, so a modifier of 1/5 reproduces the
previous slow mode exactly, and 1.0 restores normal speed.

registerProfilerCallback(), used further down the same file, still exists in
6.12 and is left alone.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/webos/developertools/plugin/src/unifiedtimerwrapper.cpp
+++ b/webos/developertools/plugin/src/unifiedtimerwrapper.cpp
@@ -30,7 +30,10 @@
 
 void UnifiedTimerWrapper::setSlowMode(bool enabled)
 {
-    QUnifiedTimer::instance()->setSlowModeEnabled(enabled);
+    // Qt 6.12 replaced setSlowModeEnabled()/setSlowdownFactor() with a single
+    // speed multiplier. Qt's old default slowdown factor was 5, so 1/5 keeps
+    // the previous behaviour; 1.0 is normal speed.
+    QUnifiedTimer::instance()->setSpeedModifier(enabled ? 0.2 : 1.0);
     m_slowMode = enabled;
     emit slowModeChanged();
 }
